selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#hold-the-coolant-area-constant-with-a-helix\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Hold the coolant area constant with a helix<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#hold-the-coolant-area-constant-with-a-helix\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>A squared channel of fixed height, rib width and count gets wider wherever the\nwall it wraps gets wider. On an engine with area ratio 8, an axial channel\nbuilt this way has more than three times the throat area at the nozzle exit. To\nkeep the area constant, wind the channel into a helix that steepens as the\nradius grows. The extra circumference then goes into the winding instead of the\nchannel width.</p><p>This guide finds that helix by root-finding the helix angle against the area\nPyskyfire computes. The result below has 40 channels, each holding the same\ncoolant area to within one part in a million from the injector to the nozzle\nexit. Drag to rotate, scroll to zoom and right-drag to pan.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/CoolingCircuit.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.CoolingCircuit\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.CoolingCircuit\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CoolingCircuit</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">contour</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cross_section</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">span</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">list</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">placement</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">channel_height</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">walls</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">coolant_transport</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roughness</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">hot_gas_surface_area_multiplier</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">outer_walls</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rib_material</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Simulation-only representation of a cooling circuit.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">walls</span></code> are ordered from hot gas to coolant. Any <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">role=\"liner\"</span></code>\nlayers precede the main layers; at least one main layer is required.\nWall-like objects without a role are treated as main layers.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin=True</span></code> enables this circuit\u2019s rib/fin heat-transfer model.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rib_material</span></code> optionally supplies its material (with <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">get_k(T)</span></code>).\nWhen omitted, the coolant-facing main-wall material is used. Disabling\nfins removes their thermal enhancement, not their channel geometry.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#root-find-the-helix-angle\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Root-find the helix angle<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#root-find-the-helix-angle\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The area at each station depends only on the helix angle at that station. One\nbuild therefore evaluates the residual at every station, and a secant step\napplied to the whole array solves them all together:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/channel_placement/SurfacePlacement.html#pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.SurfacePlacement\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.SurfacePlacement\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">SurfacePlacement</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_channel_positions</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">helix_angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">channel_angular_width</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelPlacement</span></code></p><p>Placement model for surface-mounted cooling channels.</p><p>Channels are positioned just outside the main wall stack,\noffset by total thickness and corrected for local contour angle.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/components/ThrustChamberComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.ThrustChamberComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.ThrustChamberComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ThrustChamberComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Cooling-channel surfaces with optional RegenResult fields.</p><p>Each layout seed is constructed once. Instances share its immutable mesh\nand fields and carry separate rotations and identities. No hot wall is\nconstructed. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">circuit_N.inlet/outlet</span></code> anchors refer to the first seed\u2019s\nfirst channel, at its end-section polygon centre, not a manifold port.\nEvery channel also exposes its own inlet/outlet anchors.</p><p>A circuit with a result records its coolant\u2019s CoolProp name as\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">metadata[\"fluid\"]</span></code>. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">circuit_colors</span></code> paints each circuit apart;\nwithout it every channel takes the default colour.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/common/solids/index.html#pyskyfire.common.solids.StainlessSteel304\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.common.solids.StainlessSteel304\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.common.solids.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">StainlessSteel304</span></span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/ThrustChamber.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.ThrustChamber\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.ThrustChamber\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ThrustChamber</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">contour</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cooling_circuits</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">combustion_transport</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">optimal_values</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">K_factor</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.3</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_nodes</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">50</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">h_gas_corr</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">h_cold_corr</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">compute_gas</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">film_cooling</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/FilmCooling.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.FilmCooling\" title=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.FilmCooling\"><span class=\"pre\">FilmCooling</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">keep_outs</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Simulation-only thrust-chamber assembly.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/contour/Contour.html#pyskyfire.regen.contour.Contour\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.contour.Contour\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.contour.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Contour</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">xs</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rs</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">chamber_angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">nozzle_angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Inner hot-gas contour of a bell-type rocket engine.</p><p>Represents the geometric wall line from the start of the chamber to\nthe nozzle exit, providing local areas, slopes, and radii.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>This class is used by higher-level objects such as\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">CoolingCircuit</span></code> and\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ThrustChamber</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#set-up-the-geometry\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Set up the geometry<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#set-up-the-geometry\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Write a function that builds the chamber for any helix law, and a helix law\nthat interpolates <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(\\cos\\gamma\\)</span> from a table on the solver stations. A helix law\nis a design input that requests quantities by parameter name (see\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../explanations/design-input-functions.html\"><span class=\"doc\">Design-Input Functions</span></a>), so its argument must be called\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">x</span></code>.</p>", "a[href=\"#build-the-3d-view\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Build the 3D view<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#build-the-3d-view\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Build the chamber once more with the converged law and save the scene. The\nchamber uses 400 stations and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">stride=1</span></code> draws every one of them, so the helix\nrenders cleanly where it is steepest:</p>", "a[href=\"#why-the-helix-opens-out-with-radius\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Why the helix opens out with radius<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#why-the-helix-opens-out-with-radius\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Consider <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(n\\)</span> squared channels of height <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(h\\)</span> whose floor sits at radius <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(r_b\\)</span>.\nEach channel and its share of the rib fill an annular sector. On a helix of\nangle <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(\\gamma\\)</span>, measured from the meridian, that sector\u2019s angle measured\nnormal to the channel is <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(2\\pi\\cos\\gamma/n\\)</span>. Subtracting a rib of width\n<span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(2s\\)</span>, where <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(s\\)</span> is the <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">sidewall_half_thickness</span></code>, leaves approximately</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.add\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.add\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">component</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transform</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">position</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">parent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">anchor</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">attach_to</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">tags</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">()</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"#limits\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Limits<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#limits\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"../explanations/design-input-functions.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Design-Input Functions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#design-input-functions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Most of the geometry you hand to Pyskyfire can be either a number or a\nfunction. A wall can be 1 mm thick everywhere, or it can thin out towards the\nnozzle exit. A rib can be 1 mm wide everywhere, or it can always take up a\nfifth of the local channel pitch.</p><p>A function used this way is called a <strong>design input</strong>. It declares the\nquantities it needs <em>by parameter name</em>, and Pyskyfire supplies exactly those:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/contour/index.html#pyskyfire.regen.contour.generate_contour\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.contour.generate_contour\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.contour.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">generate_contour</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">r_t</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">area_ratio</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">r_c</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">L_c</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">V_c</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">eps_c</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">AR_c</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">theta_conv</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">45</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">theta_div</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">15</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">nozzle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'rao'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">R_1f</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.5</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">R_2f</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.5</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">R_3f</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.382</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">length_fraction</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.8</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">angle_input</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'degrees'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">export_tikz</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Generate a chamber and nozzle contour using four input modes.</p><p>Exactly one of the following input combinations must be provided:</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>In the flow direction, the curvature factors occur in the order\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">R_2f</span></code> (chamber fillet), <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">R_1f</span></code> (throat entrance), then <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">R_3f</span></code>\n(throat exit). All three scale the throat radius <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">r_t</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/Wall.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.Wall\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.Wall\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Wall</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">material</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">thickness</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">role</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'main'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Single structural wall or coating layer in a thrust chamber.</p><p>Encapsulates material and thickness information for heat-conduction\ncalculations.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../explanations/channel-construction.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Physical cooling-channel construction<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#physical-cooling-channel-construction\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">build_channel_construction(circuit,</span> <span class=\"pre\">reference_path)</span></code> resolves a circuit\u2019s\nnominal winding into the section it physically occupies. The same resolved\ngeometry feeds the simulation, CAD, and the native 3D viewer, so a channel is\nsized once and drawn, meshed and solved from that one answer.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.scene.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Scene</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">title</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'Pyskyfire</span> <span class=\"pre\">3D'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">color_by</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">clim</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">show_axes</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Assemble components for desktop or standalone HTML display.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">anchor</span></code> names the added component\u2019s local anchor; <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">attach_to</span></code> is a\nworld-space Anchor. Attachment mates their outward x axes in opposition.\nIt is a one-time placement calculation, with no fluid-network constraints.\nExplicit placement and anchor placement are mutually exclusive.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">tags</span></code> labels the added node, a string or an iterable of them. Nodes\nsharing a tag appear together as one group in the HTML viewer, so a\ngrouping written into the script survives regenerating the results.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">show_axes</span></code> adds a corner orientation triad marking the scene axes\n(x red, y green, z blue). It is an orientation cue only, not a measuring\ngrid: it carries no ticks and does not indicate the origin or scale.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/cross_section/CrossSectionSquared.html#pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.CrossSectionSquared\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.CrossSectionSquared\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CrossSectionSquared</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">sidewall_half_thickness</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_points</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">8</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roof_thickness</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">floor</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'arc'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roof</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'arc'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">exposure</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelSection</span></code></p><p>Squared passages with independently straight or curved floor and roof.</p><p>sidewall_half_thickness [m] is ONE tube sidewall\u2019s normal thickness,\nequivalent to HALF the shared rib between adjacent chamber channels. A\nconstant or design-input callable is accepted. A former 1 mm full rib is\ntherefore specified as 0.5 mm here.</p><p>Floor thickness comes from SectionProfiles.t_wall. roof_thickness defaults\nto that thickness and may instead be a constant or callable. floor and roof\nindependently accept \u201carc\u201d or \u201cline\u201d. Direct width profiles use the\ndistance between internal sidewall endpoints. With sector profiles, the\nexisting constant-material-width rib construction determines those\nendpoints; choosing a line joins the same endpoints with a chord.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.save_html\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.save_html\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">save_html</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">path</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
